Interface identity root:
identity_root ID SOURCE_TYPE_CLAIM IDENTITY_FAMILY_HAS_TYPE_CLAIM WITNESS_HAS_TYPE_CLAIM_OR_INVALID COMPUTATION_RULE

The mandatory source Claim proves that the source carrier is a type. The
mandatory family Claim classifies an ordinary computed identity family by the
same admitted Universe. The optional witness Claim classifies an ordinary
proof Term by exactly that family. The computation rule must be replayed from
the source carrier and generated declaration; the root label is not authority
by itself. Exact duplicate quadruples are rejected. Registration is permitted
only after accepted-graph publication is frozen. Roots never add conversion
equations or equality reflection.

The dependency table is recomputed from the final dense rooted publication
graph. External references reachable only through accepted proof premises,
rule payloads, Contexts, or Substitutions are dependencies. External references
present only in unrooted solver or HOTT work are not dependencies.

Dense accepted proof grammar:
propositions N
proposition ID KIND AUTHORITY_KIND AUTHORITY_ID CONTEXT OPERATION SUBJECT CLASSIFIER
claims N
claim ID proposition PROPOSITION_ID
derivations N
derivation ID PROOF_KIND claim CONCLUSION_CLAIM premises PREMISE_COUNT
payload none
| payload constructor OWNER_VIEW CONSTRUCTOR_INDEX FIELD_INDEX
| payload constructor_spine OWNER_VIEW
| payload induction MATCH MOTIVE CASE_INDEX FIELD_INDEX
action SEMANTIC_ACTION_KIND SEMANTIC_ACTION_ID
premise claim CLAIM_ID action SEMANTIC_ACTION_KIND SEMANTIC_ACTION_ID
| premise scoped PROPOSITION_ID action SEMANTIC_ACTION_KIND SEMANTIC_ACTION_ID

MATCH_PATTERN_ASSUMPTION uses constructor payload.
CONSTRUCTOR_SPINE_FORMATION uses constructor_spine payload.
INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS_ELIM uses induction payload.
Every other admitted proof kind uses none payload.
Exactly one premise reference is valid. Proposition identity is serialized
once; Claims and scoped premises refer to it directly. Derivation sources are
exactly the ordered premise edges and are not repeated in a sources list.

Type declarations serialize parameter and index Contexts independently,
index count, origin, and generated source carrier. Generated identity
declarations and constructors have no invented names. Their Context telescope,
result classifier, and ordinary Term graph are authority; source readback field
metadata is absent.

Context, Substitution, Operation, Universe, interface export, debug, and
relocation records retain the v69 field meanings except that all object graph
arenas are dense. Context and Operation solver variables and source AST IDs are
not wire authority. Closure rank and lookup indices are reconstructed by
least-fixed-point replay after readback.

Observational identity fragment admitted by roots:
- closed homogeneous ordinary ADT identity families and ordinary constructor
  witnesses checked against them;
- identities of closed concrete generated-identity fibers whose source
  constructors are nullary or have only nondependent fields. Such a concrete
  fiber is treated as the source carrier of another closed ORDINARY_ADT root;
- pure Return/Thunk identity families and constructor witnesses; and
- nondependent pure Pi pointwise identity families and ordinary Lambda/Match
  witnesses whose complete accepted derivation graph replays read-only.

CONSTANT_FAMILY_LIFT and INDEXED_HIGHER_LIFT are non-empty Context actions.
Their meaning depends on an object-identity bridge and its complete boundary,
which this artifact deliberately does not persist. They are therefore not
identity-root computation rules. In particular, the eight-index square family
and its constructor telescope may be reachable implementation evidence, but a
root cannot claim that action merely by storing its result Claim and rule tag.

These roots certify only the explicitly listed type-directed computation and
inhabitance rules. They do not turn compiler-local RELATION_TYPE or TERM action
results into identity, and they do not claim completeness for contextual
equivalence. Dependent constructor fields, general dependent APP/Match/IH
action, and generic lifting through an index telescope remain residual.

The finite Universe correspondence and Universe-fiber actions are
compiler-local scaffolding. Full Universe bisimulation/coherence, generic
transport/lifting elimination, dependent telescope identity, effectful
requests/folds, host primitives, HIT, quotient, and IADT identity computation
remain residual and cannot be roots.

Dependent computation-fold verification lifecycle:
- a fold whose result family closes by deterministic pure normalization may
  contribute ordinary static typing evidence;
- blocked-effect or exhausted pure normalization creates one versioned
  COMPUTATION_FOLD_RESULT obligation keyed by the typed Operation occurrence;
- a PENDING obligation is a runtime contract and never a Claim or Derivation;
- strict compilation and Verilog admission reject PENDING obligations;
- hybrid compilation may publish PENDING obligations only when the selected
  backend declares the computation-fold result verifier and handler
  capabilities;
- artifact v70 persists only PENDING obligations. DISCHARGED and FAILED are
  execution-instance outcomes and are rejected on readback;
- execution discharges an obligation by applying its retained pure classifier
  family to the returned value and checking conversion with the continuation
  result classifier under the retained normalization profile; and
- failed discharge aborts that execution and cannot retroactively create or
  alter accepted static evidence.
Contextual equivalence is a metatheoretic adequacy target, not an artifact
record or kernel proof-search rule.
